questions.question_text:
The supplied first two stages of a car journey are straight lines joining $(0,0)$ to $(1.5,80)$ and then to $(2,80)$. Coordinates are $(\text{elapsed time in hours},\text{distance from home in km})$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1.2cm,y=0.015cm,font=\small]
% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"graph","base":[],"semantic":[]}
\definecolor{blue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{housegrid}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[housegrid,thin,xstep=0.5,ystep=20] (0,0) grid (4,200);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(4.4,0);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,220);
\node[below] at (2,-40) {Time (hours)};
\node[rotate=90] at (-0.9,100) {Distance from home (km)};
\foreach \t in {0,1,2,3,4} \node[below] at (\t,0) {$\t$};
\foreach \d in {40,80,120,160,200} \node[left] at (0,\d) {$\d$};
\draw[blue,thick] (0,0)--(1.5,80)--(2,80);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The car next travels farther from home at a constant $60$ km/h for $1$ hour $30$ minutes. Add this stage to the graph. Which description gives the line to add?
